This file lives on the ext2 disk (build/disk.img), mounted at /mnt.

Unlike tarfs (the initrd RAM filesystem), everything under /mnt is
stored in real on-disk ext2 structures: superblock, block/inode
bitmaps, inode tables with indirect blocks, and directory entries.

Writes persist across reboots -- try:

    echo hi > /mnt/hi.txt
    cat /mnt/hi.txt
    reboot   (or Ctrl-A X and re-run zig build run)
    cat /mnt/hi.txt     # still there!

The host can inspect this disk with e2fsprogs:

    debugfs -R "ls -l /" build/disk.img
    e2fsck -fn build/disk.img
